WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.752
Four bookings cover 1–3, 2–6, 8–10 and 15–18.

00:05.752 --> 00:10.610
Which busy blocks do they really form?

00:10.610 --> 00:14.700
Comparing every pair is n² work.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.010
Sort them by start instead.

00:20.010 --> 00:31.700
Once they line up, each booking only meets the block before it.

00:32.000 --> 00:40.341
2–6 starts inside 1–3, so stretch the block to 1–6.

00:40.341 --> 00:47.700
8–10 starts after 6, so it opens a new block.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.169
One sort, one walk: O(n log n).

00:52.169 --> 00:57.414
Three blocks left: 1–6, 8–10 and 15–18.

00:57.414 --> 00:59.700
That’s intervals.

